IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`
IMPORT `sfad-nocons-small-private`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, part sfad: Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (4), ss 274, 275 and 276: offers to institutional investors, accredited investors and
-- certain other persons, and the resale of securities acquired under them (lines 44138-44587 of SFA2001.txt).
-- Imports prelude, daydate, sfa-core, sfa-periods and sfad-nocons-small-private (whose list of selling or promotional expenses and prospectus limb these sections share).
--
-- How to read a function in this module: as in sfad-nocons-small-private.l4 (JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING where it does not say).
--   The investor classes of section 4A(1) are the keel's: the caller passes the keel's answer (`s 4A(1) the person is in the class of investor`, or the function for
--   paragraph (a), (b) or (c)) as an input of type MAYBE BOOLEAN. "Relevant person" is this module's own (s 275(2)).
--   Amounts the Act leaves to an order of the Authority (s 275(4)) are inputs.
--   "-- FORK" lines are collected into the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `s 274: offer made to institutional investors`

-- src:44140 | 274. Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than
-- src:44141 | section 257) do not apply to an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:44142 | derivatives contracts (whether or not they have been previously
-- src:44143 | issued) made to an institutional investor.
@ref s 274 (src:44140-44143)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, whether or not previously issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts (whether or not they have been previously issued)?
    `the person to whom the offer is made is an institutional investor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 4A(1) the person is in the class of investor` answer for the person to whom the offer is made, asked about an institutional investor (section 4A(1)(c))? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 274 the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, whether or not previously issued`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts (whether or not they have been previously issued)"
        IF `the person to whom the offer is made is an institutional investor` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "made to an institutional investor"
    -- FORK s274-1 | s 274 | `s 274 the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` | took NOTHING where the offer is not made to an institutional investor (the section grants an exemption to offers made to them and has no "if" and no "only") | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {P-c} (a scope limit with no "only")

§ `s 275(2) and (2A): the definitions`

-- src:44316 | “information memorandum” means a document —
-- src:44318 | (a) purporting to describe —
-- src:44320 | (i) the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:44321 | contracts being offered; or
-- src:44323 | (ii) the business and affairs of the person making
-- src:44324 | the offer, the issuer or (where applicable) the
-- src:44325 | underlying entity, or (where the securities or
-- src:44326 | securities‑based derivatives contracts being
-- src:44327 | offered are units or derivatives of units in a
-- src:44328 | business trust) the trustee‑manager of the
-- src:44329 | business trust or the business trust; and
-- src:44331 | (b) purporting to have been prepared for delivery to, and
-- src:44332 | review by, relevant persons and persons to whom an
-- src:44333 | offer mentioned in subsection (1A) is to be made, so
-- src:44334 | as to assist them in making an investment decision in
-- src:44335 | respect of the securities or securities‑based
-- src:44336 | derivatives contracts being offered;
@ref s 275(2) information memorandum (src:44316-44336)
GIVEN
    `the document purports to describe the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being offered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document purport to describe the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being offered?
    `the document purports to describe the business and affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity, the trustee-manager or the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document purport to describe the business and affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer or (where applicable) the underlying entity, or (where units or derivatives of units in a business trust are offered) the trustee-manager of the business trust or the business trust?
    `the document purports to have been prepared for delivery to, and review by, relevant persons and persons to whom an offer mentioned in subsection (1A) is to be made, so as to assist them in making an investment decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document purport to have been prepared for delivery to, and review by, relevant persons and persons to whom an offer mentioned in section 275(1A) is to be made, so as to assist them in making an investment decision in respect of the securities or contracts being offered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(2) the document is an information memorandum` MEANS
    IF (`the document purports to describe the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being offered` OR `the document purports to describe the business and affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity, the trustee-manager or the business trust`) AND `the document purports to have been prepared for delivery to, and review by, relevant persons and persons to whom an offer mentioned in subsection (1A) is to be made, so as to assist them in making an investment decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“information memorandum” means a document — (a) purporting to describe"

-- src:44281 | (2) In this section —
-- src:44283 | “advertisement” means —
-- src:44285 | (a) a written or printed communication;
-- src:44287 | (b) a communication by radio, television or other
-- src:44288 | medium of communication; or
-- src:44290 | (c) a communication by means of a recorded telephone
-- src:44291 | message,
-- src:44293 | that is published in connection with an offer in respect of
-- src:44294 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts, but does
-- src:44295 | not include —
-- src:44297 | (d) an information memorandum;
-- src:44299 | (e) a publication which consists solely of a disclosure,
-- src:44300 | notice or report required under this Act, or any listing
-- src:44301 | rules or other requirements of an approved exchange
-- src:44302 | or overseas exchange, which is made by any person;
-- src:44303 | or
-- src:44305 | (f) a publication which consists solely of a notice or
-- src:44306 | report of a general meeting or proposed general
-- src:44307 | meeting of the unitholders of the business trust, the
-- src:44308 | person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying
-- src:44309 | entity or any entity, or a presentation of oral or
-- src:44310 | written material on matters so contained in the notice
-- src:44311 | or report at the general meeting;
@ref s 275(2) advertisement (src:44281-44311)
GIVEN
    `the communication is a written or printed communication, a communication by radio, television or other medium of communication, or a communication by means of a recorded telephone message` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication a written or printed communication, a communication by radio, television or other medium of communication, or a communication by means of a recorded telephone message?
    `the communication is published in connection with an offer in respect of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication published in connection with an offer in respect of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the communication is an information memorandum` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 275(2) the document is an information memorandum` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under this Act, or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication a publication that consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under the Securities and Futures Act 2001, or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange, which is made by any person?
    `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting, or a presentation of material on matters so contained at the general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication a publication that consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting of the unitholders of the business trust, the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or any entity, or a presentation of oral or written material on matters so contained in the notice or report at the general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(2) the communication is an advertisement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the communication is a written or printed communication, a communication by radio, television or other medium of communication, or a communication by means of a recorded telephone message` AND `the communication is published in connection with an offer in respect of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“advertisement” means — (a) a written or printed communication; (b) a communication by radio, television or other medium of communication; or (c) a communication by means of a recorded telephone message, that is published in connection with an offer in respect of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts"
        IF (`the communication is an information memorandum` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under this Act, or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange` OR `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting, or a presentation of material on matters so contained at the general meeting`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include"
        IF `the communication is an information memorandum` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the communication is an information memorandum is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:44365 | (2A) In the definition of “information memorandum” in
-- src:44366 | subsection (2), the reference to the affairs of the person making the
-- src:44367 | offer, the issuer, the underlying entity, the trustee‑manager of the
-- src:44368 | business trust or the business trust includes —
-- src:44370 | (a) where the person making the offer, the issuer, the
-- src:44371 | underlying entity or the trustee‑manager is a corporation,
-- src:44372 | a reference to the matters mentioned in section 2(2); and
-- src:44374 | (b) in any other case, a reference to such matters as may be
-- src:44375 | prescribed by regulations made under section 341.
@ref s 275(2A) (src:44365-44375)
GIVEN
    `the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the trustee-manager is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the trustee-manager a corporation?
    `the matter is within section 2(2) as the keel answers it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 2(2) the matter is within the affairs of a corporation` answer for the matter? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the matter is one prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(2A) the matter is included in the affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity, the trustee-manager or the business trust` MEANS
    IF `the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the trustee-manager is a corporation`
    THEN `the matter is within section 2(2) as the keel answers it`
    ELSE IF `the matter is one prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such matters as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341"
    -- FORK s275-2A | s 275(2A) | `s 275(2A) the matter is included in the affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity, the trustee-manager or the business trust` | took "includes" as an extension: NOTHING for a matter that is neither within section 2(2) nor prescribed | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {IN-SHORT} ("says includes" answers NOTHING)

-- src:44338 | “relevant person” means —
-- src:44340 | (a) an accredited investor;
-- src:44342 | (b) a corporation the sole business of which is to hold
-- src:44343 | investments and the entire share capital of which is
-- src:44344 | owned by one or more individuals, each of whom is
-- src:44345 | an accredited investor;
-- src:44347 | (c) a trustee of a trust the sole purpose of which is to hold
-- src:44348 | investments and each beneficiary of which is an
-- src:44349 | individual who is an accredited investor;
-- src:44351 | (d) an officer or equivalent person of the person making
-- src:44352 | the offer (such person being an entity) or a spouse,
-- src:44353 | parent, brother, sister, son or daughter of that officer
-- src:44354 | or equivalent person; or
-- src:44356 | (e) a spouse, parent, brother, sister, son or daughter of the
-- src:44357 | person making the offer (such person being an
-- src:44358 | individual).
@ref s 275(2) relevant person (src:44338-44358)
GIVEN
    `the person is an accredited investor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 4A(1)(a) the person is an accredited investor` answer for the person? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is a corporation the sole business of which is to hold investments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation the sole business of which is to hold investments?
    `the entire share capital of the corporation is owned by one or more individuals, each of whom is an accredited investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entire share capital of the corporation owned by one or more individuals, each of whom is an accredited investor?
    `the person is the trustee of a trust the sole purpose of which is to hold investments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the trustee of a trust the sole purpose of which is to hold investments?
    `each beneficiary of the trust is an individual who is an accredited investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each beneficiary of the trust an individual who is an accredited investor?
    `the person is an officer or equivalent person of the person making the offer (such person being an entity), or a spouse, parent, brother, sister, son or daughter of that officer or equivalent person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer or equivalent person of the person making the offer (that person being an entity), or a spouse, parent, brother, sister, son or daughter of that officer or equivalent person?
    `the person is a spouse, parent, brother, sister, son or daughter of the person making the offer (such person being an individual)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a spouse, parent, brother, sister, son or daughter of the person making the offer (that person being an individual)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(2) the person is a relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person is an accredited investor` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is a corporation the sole business of which is to hold investments` AND `the entire share capital of the corporation is owned by one or more individuals, each of whom is an accredited investor`) OR (`the person is the trustee of a trust the sole purpose of which is to hold investments` AND `each beneficiary of the trust is an individual who is an accredited investor`) OR `the person is an officer or equivalent person of the person making the offer (such person being an entity), or a spouse, parent, brother, sister, son or daughter of that officer or equivalent person` OR `the person is a spouse, parent, brother, sister, son or daughter of the person making the offer (such person being an individual)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is an accredited investor` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the person is an accredited investor is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant person” means — (a) an accredited investor; (b) a corporation the sole business of which is to hold investments"

§ `s 275(1), (1A), (3), (4): offers to relevant persons, and to those who pay $200,000 or more`

-- src:44157 | (a) the offer is not accompanied by an advertisement making
-- src:44158 | an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer;
@ref s 275(1)(a) (src:44157-44158)
GIVEN
    `the offer is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer? ("Advertisement" has the meaning given by section 275(2).)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(1)(a) the offer is not accompanied by an advertisement` MEANS
    IF `the offer is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the offer is not accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:44160 | (b) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred in
-- src:44161 | connection with the offer other than those incurred for
-- src:44162 | administrative or professional services, or by way of
-- src:44163 | commission or fee for services rendered by —
-- src:44165 | (i) the holder of a capital markets services licence to
-- src:44166 | deal in capital markets products that are securities or
-- src:44167 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:44172 | (ii) an exempt person in respect of dealing in capital
-- src:44173 | markets products that are securities or
-- src:44174 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:44176 | (iii) a person who is licensed, approved, authorised or
-- src:44177 | otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or other
-- src:44178 | requirements of any foreign jurisdiction in respect of
-- src:44179 | dealing in capital markets products that are securities
-- src:44180 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts; or
-- src:44182 | (iv) a person who is exempt from the laws, codes or
-- src:44183 | requirements mentioned in sub‑paragraph (iii) in
-- src:44184 | respect of dealing in capital markets products that are
-- src:44185 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:44186 | and
@ref s 275(1)(b) (src:44160-44186)
GIVEN
    `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the offer` IS A LIST OF `s 272A(1)(d) kind of selling or promotional expense` @desc What are the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the offer? (An empty list: none are paid or incurred.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(1)(b) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred other than those the paragraph allows` MEANS
    `s 272A(1)(d) the selling or promotional expenses are ones the exemption allows` `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the offer`

-- src:44188 | (c) no prospectus in respect of the offer has been registered by
-- src:44189 | the Authority or, where a prospectus has been registered —
-- src:44191 | (i) the prospectus has expired pursuant to section 250;
-- src:44192 | or
-- src:44194 | (ii) the person making the offer has before making the
-- src:44195 | offer —
-- src:44197 | (A) informed the Authority by written notice of its
-- src:44198 | intent to make the offer in reliance on the
-- src:44199 | exemption under this subsection; and
-- src:44201 | (B) taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the
-- src:44202 | person to whom the offer is made that the offer
-- src:44203 | is made in reliance on the exemption under this
-- src:44204 | subsection.
@ref s 275(1)(c) (src:44188-44204)
GIVEN
    `a prospectus in respect of the offer has been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered a prospectus in respect of the offer?
    `the prospectus has expired under section 250` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prospectus expired pursuant to section 250? (Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (2), another part's answer.)
    `the person making the offer has before making the offer informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer, before making the offer, informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under section 275(1)?
    `the person making the offer has before making the offer taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the person to whom the offer is made that the offer is made in reliance on the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer, before making the offer, taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the person to whom the offer is made that the offer is made in reliance on the exemption under section 275(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(1)(c) no prospectus is registered, or the registered prospectus has expired or the Authority and the offeree have been told` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a prospectus in respect of the offer has been registered by the Authority`) OR `the prospectus has expired under section 250` OR (`the person making the offer has before making the offer informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under this subsection` AND `the person making the offer has before making the offer taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the person to whom the offer is made that the offer is made in reliance on the exemption`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no prospectus in respect of the offer has been registered by the Authority or, where a prospectus has been registered"

-- src:44151 | 275.—(1) Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other
-- src:44152 | than section 257) do not apply to an offer of securities or
-- src:44153 | securities‑based derivatives contracts, whether or not they have
-- src:44154 | been previously issued, where the offer is made to a relevant person,
-- src:44155 | if —
@ref s 275(1) (src:44151-44155)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, whether or not previously issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts (whether or not they have been previously issued)?
    `the person to whom the offer is made is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 275(2) the person is a relevant person` answer for the person to whom the offer is made? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (a), no advertisement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 275(1)(a) the offer is not accompanied by an advertisement` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (b), the selling or promotional expenses` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 275(1)(b) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred other than those the paragraph allows` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (c), the prospectus` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 275(1)(c) no prospectus is registered, or the registered prospectus has expired or the Authority and the offeree have been told` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, whether or not previously issued`) OR (`the person to whom the offer is made is a relevant person` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the offer is made to a relevant person"
        IF (`paragraph (a), no advertisement` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (b), the selling or promotional expenses` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (c), the prospectus` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts, whether or not they have been previously issued, where the offer is made to a relevant person, if"
        IF (`the person to whom the offer is made is a relevant person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (a), no advertisement` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (b), the selling or promotional expenses` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (c), the prospectus` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the person or a paragraph is not answered
    -- FORK s275-1 | s 275(1) | `s 275(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` | took NOTHING where the offer is not made to a relevant person (the "where" names the scope of the exemption, with no "only") and JUST FALSE where a paragraph (a), (b) or (c) fails (conditions of an "if") | other reading JUST FALSE for a non-relevant person and NOTHING for a failed paragraph | licence {P-c} for the first and {IN-SHORT} for the second; the second is under "Marginal readings for a lawyer"

-- src:44220 | (a) the offer is on terms that the securities or securities‑based
-- src:44221 | derivatives contracts may only be acquired at a
-- src:44222 | consideration of not less than $200,000 (or its equivalent
-- src:44223 | in a foreign currency) for each transaction, whether such
-- src:44224 | amount is to be paid for in cash or by exchange of
-- src:44225 | securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or other
-- src:44226 | assets;
@ref s 275(1A)(a) (src:44220-44226)
GIVEN
    `the least consideration at which the offer allows the securities or contracts to be acquired for each transaction, in Singapore dollars or the equivalent in a foreign currency` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the least consideration at which the terms of the offer allow the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to be acquired for each transaction, whether paid in cash or by exchange of securities, contracts or other assets, in Singapore dollars or the equivalent in a foreign currency?
    `the Authority has specified another amount by order in the Gazette in substitution for $200,000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by order in the Gazette, specified another amount in substitution for $200,000 (section 275(4))?
    `the other amount the Authority has specified in substitution` IS A NUMBER @desc What other amount has the Authority specified in substitution for $200,000, in the same currency? (Put 0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(1A)(a) the offer is on terms that the securities or contracts may only be acquired at a consideration of not less than the amount for each transaction` MEANS
    IF `the least consideration at which the offer allows the securities or contracts to be acquired for each transaction, in Singapore dollars or the equivalent in a foreign currency` AT LEAST (`s 275(4) the amount that applies in place of $200,000` `the Authority has specified another amount by order in the Gazette in substitution for $200,000` `the other amount the Authority has specified in substitution`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the offer is on terms that the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts may only be acquired at a consideration of not less than $200,000"

-- src:44392 | (4) The Authority may, by order in the Gazette, specify an amount
-- src:44393 | in substitution of any amount specified in subsection (1A)(a).
@ref s 275(4) (src:44392-44393)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has specified another amount by order in the Gazette in substitution for $200,000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by order in the Gazette, specified another amount in substitution for $200,000 (section 275(4))?
    `the other amount the Authority has specified in substitution` IS A NUMBER @desc What other amount has the Authority specified in substitution for $200,000, in the same currency? (Put 0 if none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 275(4) the amount that applies in place of $200,000` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has specified another amount by order in the Gazette in substitution for $200,000`
    THEN `the other amount the Authority has specified in substitution`
    ELSE 200000

-- src:44228 | (b) the offer is not accompanied by an advertisement making
-- src:44229 | an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer;
@ref s 275(1A)(b) (src:44228-44229)
GIVEN
    `the offer is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer? ("Advertisement" has the meaning given by section 275(2).)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(1A)(b) the offer is not accompanied by an advertisement` MEANS
    IF `the offer is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the offer is not accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:44231 | (c) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred in
-- src:44232 | connection with the offer other than those incurred for
-- src:44233 | administrative or professional services, or by way of
-- src:44234 | commission or fee for services rendered by —
-- src:44236 | (i) the holder of a capital markets services licence to
-- src:44237 | deal in capital markets products that are securities or
-- src:44238 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:44240 | (ii) an exempt person in respect of dealing in capital
-- src:44241 | markets products that are securities or
-- src:44242 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:44244 | (iii) a person who is licensed, approved, authorised or
-- src:44245 | otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or other
-- src:44246 | requirements of any foreign jurisdiction in respect of
-- src:44247 | dealing in capital markets products that are securities
-- src:44248 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts; or
-- src:44250 | (iv) a person who is exempt from the laws, codes or
-- src:44251 | requirements mentioned in sub‑paragraph (iii) in
-- src:44252 | respect of dealing in capital markets products that are
-- src:44253 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:44254 | and
@ref s 275(1A)(c) (src:44231-44254)
GIVEN
    `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the offer` IS A LIST OF `s 272A(1)(d) kind of selling or promotional expense` @desc What are the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the offer? (An empty list: none are paid or incurred.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(1A)(c) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred other than those the paragraph allows` MEANS
    `s 272A(1)(d) the selling or promotional expenses are ones the exemption allows` `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the offer`

-- src:44256 | (d) no prospectus in respect of the offer has been registered by
-- src:44257 | the Authority or, where a prospectus has been registered —
-- src:44259 | (i) the prospectus has expired pursuant to section 250;
-- src:44260 | or
-- src:44265 | (ii) the person making the offer has before making the
-- src:44266 | offer —
-- src:44268 | (A) informed the Authority by written notice of its
-- src:44269 | intent to make the offer in reliance on the
-- src:44270 | exemption under this subsection; and
-- src:44272 | (B) taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the
-- src:44273 | person to whom the offer is made that the offer
-- src:44274 | is made in reliance on the exemption under this
-- src:44275 | subsection.
@ref s 275(1A)(d) (src:44256-44275)
GIVEN
    `a prospectus in respect of the offer has been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered a prospectus in respect of the offer?
    `the prospectus has expired under section 250` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prospectus expired pursuant to section 250? (Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (2), another part's answer.)
    `the person making the offer has before making the offer informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer, before making the offer, informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under section 275(1A)?
    `the person making the offer has before making the offer taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the person to whom the offer is made that the offer is made in reliance on the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer, before making the offer, taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the person to whom the offer is made that the offer is made in reliance on the exemption under section 275(1A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(1A)(d) no prospectus is registered, or the registered prospectus has expired or the Authority and the offeree have been told` MEANS
    `s 275(1)(c) no prospectus is registered, or the registered prospectus has expired or the Authority and the offeree have been told` `a prospectus in respect of the offer has been registered by the Authority` `the prospectus has expired under section 250` `the person making the offer has before making the offer informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under this subsection` `the person making the offer has before making the offer taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the person to whom the offer is made that the offer is made in reliance on the exemption`

-- src:44210 | (1A) Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than
-- src:44211 | section 257) do not apply to an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:44212 | derivatives contracts to a person who acquires the securities or
-- src:44213 | securities‑based derivatives contracts as principal, whether or not the
-- src:44214 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts have been
-- src:44215 | previously issued, if —
@ref s 275(1A) (src:44210-44215)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, whether or not previously issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts (whether or not they have been previously issued)?
    `the person to whom the offer is made acquires the securities or contracts as principal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person to whom the offer is made acquire the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts as principal?
    `paragraph (a), the consideration for each transaction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 275(1A)(a) the offer is on terms that the securities or contracts may only be acquired at a consideration of not less than the amount for each transaction` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (b), no advertisement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 275(1A)(b) the offer is not accompanied by an advertisement` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (c), the selling or promotional expenses` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 275(1A)(c) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred other than those the paragraph allows` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (d), the prospectus` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 275(1A)(d) no prospectus is registered, or the registered prospectus has expired or the Authority and the offeree have been told` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(1A) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the offer is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, whether or not previously issued`) OR (NOT `the person to whom the offer is made acquires the securities or contracts as principal`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts to a person who acquires the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts as principal"
        IF (`paragraph (a), the consideration for each transaction` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (b), no advertisement` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (c), the selling or promotional expenses` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (d), the prospectus` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whether or not the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts have been previously issued, if"
        IF (`paragraph (a), the consideration for each transaction` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (b), no advertisement` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (c), the selling or promotional expenses` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (d), the prospectus` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a paragraph is not answered
    -- FORK s275-1A | s 275(1A) | `s 275(1A) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` | took NOTHING where the person does not acquire as principal (the scope of the exemption, with no "only") and JUST FALSE where a paragraph (a) to (d) fails | other reading as for section 275(1) | licence {P-c} and {IN-SHORT}; under "Marginal readings for a lawyer"

-- src:44379 | (3) Despite any condition in section 99 or any regulation made for
-- src:44380 | the purposes of that section that a person has to deal in capital markets
-- src:44381 | products that are securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:44382 | for the person’s own account with or through a person prescribed by
-- src:44383 | the Authority so that the firstmentioned person can qualify as an
-- src:44384 | exempt person, a person who acquires securities or securities‑based
-- src:44385 | derivatives contracts under an offer made in reliance on an exemption
-- src:44386 | under section 274 or subsection (1) or (1A) for the person’s own
-- src:44387 | account is treated as an exempt person even though the person does
-- src:44388 | not comply with that condition.
@ref s 275(3) (src:44379-44388)
GIVEN
    `the person acquires securities or contracts under an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or section 275(1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person acquire securities or securities-based derivatives contracts under an offer made in reliance on the exemption under section 274 or section 275(1) or (1A)?
    `the person acquires them for the person's own account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person acquire them for the person's own account?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(3) the person is treated as an exempt person` MEANS
    IF `the person acquires securities or contracts under an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or section 275(1) or (1A)` AND `the person acquires them for the person's own account`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who acquires securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts under an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or subsection (1) or (1A) for the person’s own account is treated as an exempt person"

§ `s 276: offer of securities acquired pursuant to section 274 or 275`

-- src:44537 | (7) Subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply where the securities or
-- src:44538 | securities-based derivatives contracts that are acquired are —
-- src:44540 | (a) securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a
-- src:44541 | corporation that are of the same class as other securities or
-- src:44542 | securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation,
-- src:44543 | and —
-- src:44545 | (i) those other securities or securities-based derivatives
-- src:44546 | contracts are listed for quotation on an approved
-- src:44547 | exchange; and
-- src:44549 | (ii) a prospectus, offer information statement,
-- src:44550 | introductory document, shareholders’ circular for a
-- src:44551 | reverse take-over, document issued for the purposes
-- src:44552 | of a scheme of arrangement, or any other similar
-- src:44553 | document approved by an approved exchange, had
-- src:44554 | earlier been issued in connection with —
-- src:44556 | (A) an offer of those other securities or securities-
-- src:44557 | based derivatives contracts; or
-- src:44559 | (B) the listing for quotation of those other
-- src:44560 | securities or securities-based derivatives
-- src:44561 | contracts; or
-- src:44566 | (b) units in a business trust or derivatives of units in a business
-- src:44567 | trust that are of the same class as other units in the business
-- src:44568 | trust or derivatives of units in the business trust, and —
-- src:44570 | (i) those other units or derivatives of units are listed for
-- src:44571 | quotation on an approved exchange; and
-- src:44573 | (ii) a prospectus, offer information statement,
-- src:44574 | introductory document, shareholders’ circular for a
-- src:44575 | reverse take-over, document issued for the purposes
-- src:44576 | of a scheme of arrangement, or any other similar
-- src:44577 | document approved by an approved exchange, had
-- src:44578 | earlier been issued in connection with —
-- src:44580 | (A) an offer of those other units or derivatives of
-- src:44581 | units; or
-- src:44583 | (B) the listing for quotation of those other units or
-- src:44584 | derivatives of units.
@ref s 276(7) (src:44537-44584)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts are of a corporation and are of the same class as other securities or contracts of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or contracts acquired securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation that are of the same class as other securities or contracts of the corporation?
    `the units are units in a business trust or derivatives of units in a business trust of the same class as other units or derivatives of units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the units acquired units in a business trust, or derivatives of units in a business trust, that are of the same class as other units in the business trust or derivatives of units in the business trust?
    `those other securities, contracts, units or derivatives are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those other securities, contracts, units or derivatives listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
    `a prospectus, offer information statement, introductory document, shareholders' circular for a reverse take-over, document issued for a scheme of arrangement, or similar document approved by an approved exchange, had earlier been issued in connection with an offer of those other securities or their listing for quotation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had a prospectus, offer information statement, introductory document, shareholders' circular for a reverse take-over, document issued for the purposes of a scheme of arrangement, or any other similar document approved by an approved exchange, earlier been issued in connection with an offer of those other securities, contracts, units or derivatives, or their listing for quotation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(7) subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply to the securities or contracts acquired` MEANS
    IF (`the securities or contracts are of a corporation and are of the same class as other securities or contracts of the corporation` OR `the units are units in a business trust or derivatives of units in a business trust of the same class as other units or derivatives of units`) AND `those other securities, contracts, units or derivatives are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` AND `a prospectus, offer information statement, introductory document, shareholders' circular for a reverse take-over, document issued for a scheme of arrangement, or similar document approved by an approved exchange, had earlier been issued in connection with an offer of those other securities or their listing for quotation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply where the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts that are acquired are"
    -- FORK s276-7 | s 276(7) | `s 276(7) subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply to the securities or contracts acquired` | took NOTHING where the securities are not of the kinds (a) or (b) (the flat "do not apply" is limited to those cases) | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {P-c}. The text's paragraphs (a) and (b) are alternatives for a corporation's securities and a business trust's units: the first two inputs ask which of them the securities are, and the other two inputs are the same for both.

-- src:44424 | (1A) The reference to the sale of securities or securities‑based
-- src:44425 | derivatives contracts under subsection (1) includes —
-- src:44427 | (a) where the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:44428 | contracts initially acquired are debentures, or units of
-- src:44429 | shares or debentures, with an attached right of conversion
-- src:44430 | into shares or debentures, a reference to the sale of the
-- src:44431 | converted shares or debentures; and
-- src:44433 | (b) where the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:44434 | contracts initially acquired are derivatives of units in a
-- src:44435 | business trust, with an attached right of conversion into
-- src:44436 | units in the business trust, a reference to the sale of the
-- src:44437 | units in the business trust.
@ref s 276(1A) (src:44424-44437)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts initially acquired are debentures, or units of shares or debentures, with an attached right of conversion into shares or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or contracts initially acquired debentures, or units of shares or debentures, with an attached right of conversion into shares or debentures?
    `the converted shares or debentures are sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the converted shares or debentures sold?
    `the securities or contracts initially acquired are derivatives of units in a business trust with an attached right of conversion into units in the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or contracts initially acquired derivatives of units in a business trust, with an attached right of conversion into units in the business trust?
    `the units in the business trust are sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the units in the business trust sold?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(1A) the sale of the converted securities is a sale for subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF (`the securities or contracts initially acquired are debentures, or units of shares or debentures, with an attached right of conversion into shares or debentures` AND `the converted shares or debentures are sold`) OR (`the securities or contracts initially acquired are derivatives of units in a business trust with an attached right of conversion into units in the business trust` AND `the units in the business trust are sold`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The reference to the sale of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts under subsection (1) includes"

-- src:44397 | 276.—(1) Despite sections 272A, 272B, 273(1)(d), (da), (e), (ea),
-- src:44398 | (f), (g), (h), (i), (ia), (j) and (k), 277, 278 and 279 but subject to
-- src:44399 | subsection (7), where securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:44400 | contracts initially acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on
-- src:44401 | an exemption under section 274 or 275 are sold within the period of
-- src:44402 | 6 months from the date of the initial acquisition to any person other
-- src:44403 | than —
-- src:44405 | (a) an institutional investor;
-- src:44407 | (b) a relevant person as defined in section 275(2); or
-- src:44409 | (c) any person pursuant to an offer referred to in
-- src:44410 | section 275(1A),
-- src:44415 | then Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division apply to the offer
-- src:44416 | resulting in that sale.
@ref s 276(1) (src:44397-44416)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts were initially acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts initially acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275?
    `the securities or contracts are sold, counting the sale of converted securities as subsection (1A) says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or contracts sold (counting, for debentures or units with a right of conversion, the sale of the converted securities as section 276(1A) says)?
    `the day of the initial acquisition` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the securities or contracts initially acquired?
    `the day of the sale` IS A DATE @desc On what day are they sold?
    `the sale is to an institutional investor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 4A(1) the person is in the class of investor` answer for the buyer, asked about an institutional investor? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the sale is to a relevant person as defined in section 275(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 275(2) the person is a relevant person` answer for the buyer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the sale is to a person pursuant to an offer referred to in section 275(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sale made to a person pursuant to an offer referred to in section 275(1A)?
    `subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply by subsection (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 276(7) subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply to the securities or contracts acquired` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(1) Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division apply to the offer resulting in the sale` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the securities or contracts were initially acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275` AND `the securities or contracts are sold, counting the sale of converted securities as subsection (1A) says`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts initially acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275 are sold"
        IF `subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply by subsection (7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply where the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts that are acquired are"
        IF (`the day of the sale` GREATER THAN (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the initial acquisition` 6 Months)) OR (`the day of the sale` LESS THAN `the day of the initial acquisition`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are sold within the period of 6 months from the date of the initial acquisition"
        IF (`the sale is to an institutional investor` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the sale is to a relevant person as defined in section 275(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the sale is to a person pursuant to an offer referred to in section 275(1A)`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to any person other than — (a) an institutional investor; (b) a relevant person as defined in section 275(2); or (c) any person pursuant to an offer referred to in section 275(1A)"
        IF (`the sale is to an institutional investor` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the sale is to a relevant person as defined in section 275(2)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply by subsection (7)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the buyer's class, or whether subsection (7) applies, is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- FORK s276-1 | s 276(1) | `s 276(1) Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division apply to the offer resulting in the sale` | took JUST FALSE where the sale is outside the 6 months (a period the text fixes in its own words), where subsection (7) applies, or where the buyer is one of the three excepted persons ("other than"); took NOTHING where the securities were not acquired under section 274 or 275 or were not sold; took the 6 months as ending on the day 6 months after the day of acquisition (the keel's P1 and P4) | other reading NOTHING outside the 6 months (the text does not say the Subdivisions do not apply then) | licence {P-a} and the delegated-definitions ruling's item (c) ("when" counts as "where"); under "Marginal readings for a lawyer". The opening "Despite sections 272A, 272B, 273(1)(d) ... 277, 278 and 279" is the reason the answer is JUST TRUE even when another exemption would otherwise cover the offer: the caller does not state those exemptions here.

-- src:44441 | (2) Where securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:44442 | initially acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an
-- src:44443 | exemption under section 274 or 275 are sold to —
-- src:44445 | (a) an institutional investor;
-- src:44447 | (b) a relevant person as defined in section 275(2); or
-- src:44449 | (c) any person pursuant to an offer referred to in
-- src:44450 | section 275(1A),
-- src:44452 | Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division do not apply to the
-- src:44453 | offer resulting in that sale.
@ref s 276(2) (src:44441-44453)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts were initially acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts initially acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275?
    `the sale is to an institutional investor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 4A(1) the person is in the class of investor` answer for the buyer, asked about an institutional investor? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the sale is to a relevant person as defined in section 275(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 275(2) the person is a relevant person` answer for the buyer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the sale is to a person pursuant to an offer referred to in section 275(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sale made to a person pursuant to an offer referred to in section 275(1A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(2) Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division do not apply to the offer resulting in the sale` MEANS
    IF `the securities or contracts were initially acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275` AND ((`the sale is to an institutional investor` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the sale is to a relevant person as defined in section 275(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the sale is to a person pursuant to an offer referred to in section 275(1A)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "are sold to — (a) an institutional investor; (b) a relevant person as defined in section 275(2); or (c) any person pursuant to an offer referred to in section 275(1A)"

-- src:44459 | (3) Subject to subsection (7), securities or securities‑based
-- src:44460 | derivatives contracts of a corporation (other than a corporation that
-- src:44461 | is an accredited investor) —
-- src:44463 | (a) the sole business of which is to hold investments; and
-- src:44468 | (b) the entire share capital of which is owned by one or more
-- src:44469 | individuals, each of whom is an accredited investor,
-- src:44471 | must not be transferred within 6 months after the corporation has
-- src:44472 | acquired any securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:44473 | pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under
-- src:44474 | section 275 unless —
-- src:44476 | (c) that transfer —
-- src:44478 | (i) is made only to institutional investors or relevant
-- src:44479 | persons as defined in section 275(2); or
-- src:44481 | (ii) arises from an offer referred to in section 275(1A);
-- src:44483 | (d) no consideration is or will be given for the transfer; or
-- src:44485 | (e) the transfer is by operation of law. [2/2009; 4/2017]
@ref s 276(3) (src:44459-44485)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts are of a corporation, other than a corporation that is an accredited investor, the sole business of which is to hold investments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or contracts those of a corporation (other than a corporation that is an accredited investor) the sole business of which is to hold investments?
    `the entire share capital of the corporation is owned by one or more individuals, each of whom is an accredited investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entire share capital of the corporation owned by one or more individuals, each of whom is an accredited investor?
    `the corporation has acquired securities or contracts pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 275` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation acquired securities or securities-based derivatives contracts pursuant to an offer made in reliance on the exemption under section 275?
    `the day the corporation acquired the securities or contracts` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation acquire the securities or contracts?
    `the day of the transfer` IS A DATE @desc On what day are the securities or contracts transferred?
    `the transfer is made only to institutional investors or relevant persons as defined in section 275(2), or arises from an offer referred to in section 275(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer made only to institutional investors or relevant persons as defined in section 275(2), or does it arise from an offer referred to in section 275(1A)?
    `no consideration is or will be given for the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is, or will, any consideration be given for the transfer? (Answer yes here if none is.)
    `the transfer is by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer by operation of law?
    `subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply by subsection (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 276(7) subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply to the securities or contracts acquired` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(3) the transfer of the securities or contracts of the investment-holding corporation is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the securities or contracts are of a corporation, other than a corporation that is an accredited investor, the sole business of which is to hold investments` AND `the entire share capital of the corporation is owned by one or more individuals, each of whom is an accredited investor` AND `the corporation has acquired securities or contracts pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 275`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of a corporation (other than a corporation that is an accredited investor) — (a) the sole business of which is to hold investments; and (b) the entire share capital of which is owned by one or more individuals, each of whom is an accredited investor"
        IF `subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply by subsection (7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply where the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts that are acquired are"
        IF (`the day of the transfer` GREATER THAN (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the corporation acquired the securities or contracts` 6 Months)) OR (`the day of the transfer` LESS THAN `the day the corporation acquired the securities or contracts`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be transferred within 6 months after the corporation has acquired any securities"
        IF `the transfer is made only to institutional investors or relevant persons as defined in section 275(2), or arises from an offer referred to in section 275(1A)` OR `no consideration is or will be given for the transfer` OR `the transfer is by operation of law`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless — (c) that transfer — (i) is made only to institutional investors or relevant persons as defined in section 275(2); or (ii) arises from an offer referred to in section 275(1A); (d) no consideration is or will be given for the transfer; or (e) the transfer is by operation of law"
        IF `subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply by subsection (7)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether subsection (7) applies is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- FORK s276-3 | s 276(3) | `s 276(3) the transfer of the securities or contracts of the investment-holding corporation is barred` | took the bar as a decision function (JUST TRUE: the transfer is barred) because the text names no party who "must not" transfer; JUST FALSE once an "unless" exception (c), (d) or (e) is met or after the 6 months, NOTHING where the corporation is not of the kind described | other reading NOTHING once an exception is met | licence {CC} (an "unless" once met) and {P-a}; no regulative rule is written for it (no party is named): listed under "Rules with no breach path (sfad)"

-- src:44486 | (4) Subject to subsection (7), where —
-- src:44488 | (a) the sole purpose of a trust (other than a trust the trustee of
-- src:44489 | which is an accredited investor) is to hold investments; and
-- src:44491 | (b) each beneficiary of the trust is an individual who is an
-- src:44492 | accredited investor,
-- src:44494 | the beneficiaries’ rights and interest (howsoever described) in the
-- src:44495 | trust must not be transferred within 6 months after securities or
-- src:44496 | securities‑based derivatives contracts are acquired for the trust
-- src:44497 | pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under
-- src:44498 | section 275 unless —
-- src:44500 | (c) that transfer —
-- src:44502 | (i) is made only to institutional investors or relevant
-- src:44503 | persons as defined in section 275(2); or
-- src:44505 | (ii) arises from an offer that is made on terms that such
-- src:44506 | rights or interest are acquired at a consideration of
-- src:44507 | not less than $200,000 (or its equivalent in a foreign
-- src:44508 | currency) for each transaction, whether such amount
-- src:44509 | is to be paid for in cash or by exchange of securities
-- src:44510 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts or other
-- src:44511 | assets;
-- src:44516 | (d) no consideration is or will be given for the transfer; or
-- src:44518 | (e) the transfer is by operation of law.
@ref s 276(4) (src:44486-44518)
GIVEN
    `the sole purpose of the trust, the trustee of which is not an accredited investor, is to hold investments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sole purpose of the trust (other than a trust the trustee of which is an accredited investor) to hold investments?
    `each beneficiary of the trust is an individual who is an accredited investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each beneficiary of the trust an individual who is an accredited investor? (Section 276(5): beneficiaries include unitholders of a business trust and participants of a collective investment scheme.)
    `securities or contracts have been acquired for the trust pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 275` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have securities or securities-based derivatives contracts been acquired for the trust pursuant to an offer made in reliance on the exemption under section 275?
    `the day the securities or contracts were acquired for the trust` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the securities or contracts acquired for the trust?
    `the day of the transfer` IS A DATE @desc On what day are the beneficiaries' rights and interest transferred?
    `the transfer is made only to institutional investors or relevant persons as defined in section 275(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer made only to institutional investors or relevant persons as defined in section 275(2)?
    `the transfer arises from an offer made on terms that the rights or interest are acquired at a consideration of not less than $200,000 for each transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the transfer arise from an offer made on terms that the rights or interest are acquired at a consideration of not less than $200,000 (or its equivalent in a foreign currency) for each transaction, whether paid in cash or by exchange of securities, contracts or other assets?
    `no consideration is or will be given for the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is, or will, any consideration be given for the transfer? (Answer yes here if none is.)
    `the transfer is by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transfer by operation of law?
    `subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply by subsection (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 276(7) subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply to the securities or contracts acquired` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(4) the transfer of the beneficiaries' rights and interest in the trust is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the sole purpose of the trust, the trustee of which is not an accredited investor, is to hold investments` AND `each beneficiary of the trust is an individual who is an accredited investor` AND `securities or contracts have been acquired for the trust pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 275`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where — (a) the sole purpose of a trust (other than a trust the trustee of which is an accredited investor) is to hold investments; and (b) each beneficiary of the trust is an individual who is an accredited investor"
        IF `subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply by subsection (7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply where the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts that are acquired are"
        IF (`the day of the transfer` GREATER THAN (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the securities or contracts were acquired for the trust` 6 Months)) OR (`the day of the transfer` LESS THAN `the day the securities or contracts were acquired for the trust`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be transferred within 6 months after securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts are acquired for the trust"
        IF `the transfer is made only to institutional investors or relevant persons as defined in section 275(2)` OR `the transfer arises from an offer made on terms that the rights or interest are acquired at a consideration of not less than $200,000 for each transaction` OR `no consideration is or will be given for the transfer` OR `the transfer is by operation of law`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless — (c) that transfer — (i) is made only to institutional investors or relevant persons as defined in section 275(2); or (ii) arises from an offer that is made on terms that such rights or interest are acquired at a consideration of not less than $200,000"
        IF `subsections (1), (3) and (4) do not apply by subsection (7)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether subsection (7) applies is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- FORK s276-4 | s 276(4) | `s 276(4) the transfer of the beneficiaries' rights and interest in the trust is barred` | took the bar as a decision function (no party is named), JUST FALSE once an "unless" exception holds or after the 6 months, NOTHING outside the trusts described | other reading NOTHING once an exception holds | licence {CC} and {P-a}; the $200,000 of paragraph (c)(ii) is not subject to the Authority's order under section 275(4), which speaks only of subsection (1A)(a); the caller states whether the offer's terms met $200,000

-- src:44522 | (5) To avoid doubt, the reference to beneficiaries in subsection (4)
-- src:44523 | includes a reference to unitholders of a business trust and participants
-- src:44524 | of a collective investment scheme.
@ref s 276(5) (src:44522-44524)
GIVEN
    `the person is a unitholder of a business trust or a participant of a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a unitholder of a business trust, or a participant of a collective investment scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(5) the person is a beneficiary for subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a unitholder of a business trust or a participant of a collective investment scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to beneficiaries in subsection (4) includes a reference to unitholders of a business trust and participants of a collective investment scheme"

-- src:44526 | (6) To avoid doubt, where any securities or securities‑based
-- src:44527 | derivatives contracts are acquired pursuant to an offer made in
-- src:44528 | reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275, an offer to sell
-- src:44529 | those securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts may be made
-- src:44530 | in reliance on an exemption under section 273(1)(d), (da), (e) or (ea)
-- src:44531 | after 6 months have elapsed from the date of the firstmentioned offer.
@ref s 276(6) (src:44526-44531)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts were acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275?
    `the day of the firstmentioned offer` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offer under section 274 or 275 made?
    `the day of the offer to sell` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the offer to sell those securities or contracts made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(6) an offer to sell may be made in reliance on section 273(1)(d), (da), (e) or (ea)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the securities or contracts were acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where any securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts are acquired pursuant to an offer made in reliance on an exemption under section 274 or 275"
        IF `the day of the offer to sell` GREATER THAN (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the firstmentioned offer` 6 Months)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offer to sell those securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts may be made in reliance on an exemption under section 273(1)(d), (da), (e) or (ea) after 6 months have elapsed from the date of the firstmentioned offer"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
    -- FORK s276-6 | s 276(6) | `s 276(6) an offer to sell may be made in reliance on section 273(1)(d), (da), (e) or (ea)` | took JUST FALSE before the 6 months have elapsed: the gate "after 6 months have elapsed" is a period the text fixes in its own words (the periods ruling's item (a)) | other reading NOTHING (a grant limited by its own wording, the "In short" sentence and limit 1 of the grant ruling) | licence {P-a}; {G3} says to list a "may" function gated in this way and not to change it: this is the split site (ii) of the brief. The section is a "to avoid doubt" clarification.
